.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt NOVI-VOLUME 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm novi-volume
.Nd change the playback volume
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm up | down Op Ar step
.Nm
.Cm mute | get | control
.Nm
.Cm set Ar percent
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a front end to
.Xr amixer 1 .
It is bound to the XF86Audio keys by the compositor, and those
bindings fire even while the session is locked: changing the volume
discloses nothing, and refusing would mean you could not silence a
machine you had just locked and walked away from.
.Bl -tag -width "up|down [step]"
.It Cm up | down Op Ar step
Louder or quieter.
.Ar step
is a percentage, 5 by default.
.Cm up
unmutes;
.Cm down
deliberately does not, because unmuting on the way down makes the
quiet key briefly loud.
.It Cm mute
Toggle mute.
.It Cm set Ar percent
Set the volume.
.It Cm get
Print
.Ar percent Ar muted Ar control ,
where
.Ar muted
is 0 or 1.
.It Cm control
Print the mixer control this machine uses.
.El
.Ss Which control
The control is chosen rather than assumed.
.Nm
prefers Master, PCM, Speaker or Headphone and otherwise takes the
first control ALSA reports with
.Sy pvolume
in its capabilities: a control with only
.Sy pswitch
is a mute toggle with nothing to turn.
Hardcoding
.Dq Master
works on every real machine and fails on emulated cards that invent
their own names.
.Ss Reading back
.Cm set Ar n
does not always read back
.Ar n .
A percentage is a position in the card's own raw range, so 40 on a
64-step control lands on 41.
.Cm get
prints what the card holds, never what was asked for.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/run/novi/volume" -compact
.It Pa /run/novi/volume
The published reading.
The panel reads this file rather than forking
.Xr amixer 1
once a second, so
.Xr amixer 1
run by hand is not reflected until the next
.Nm
call.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr novi-state 1
.Sh CAVEATS
A machine with no sound card says so and exits non-zero.
